1 (a or b) is the easiest to understand from my perspective.  The explicit declaration of "real" to distinguish between bounds and sizes seems like the most natural for someone using the language for the first time -- 3c is just asking for a new user to mix up the indices and start sampling a scalar with support between 3 and 4.

> We need to decide so I can carry on refactoring the
> models!.  Let me renumber the standing proposals:
>
> 1.   a.  matrix<3,4,real[0,1]> x;
>     b.  matrix<real[0,1]>[3,4] x;
>
> 2.   a.  matrix<3,4>[0,1] x;
>     b.  matrix(3,4)[0,1] x;
>     c.  matrix[3,4][0,1] x;
>
> 3.   a.  matrix_bounded[0,1]<3,4>;
>     b.  matrix_bounded[0,1](3,4);
>     c.  matrix_bounded[0,1][3,4];
>
> Now that I finished the message, I'm leaning toward 1.b. myself
> as a first choice, and 3c. as a second.
>
> - Bob

