I did the global search and replace on both the
doc and all the models.  The unit tests now all work
again.  I skimmed an output report and did some other
investigations and I think the models should now all be
OK, too.

The new syntax for dimension declarations, interval
constraints, and truncated probability functions is as
follows:

    real  a[3,4,5];

    vector[4]  b;

    matrix[4,5] c;

    real[-1,1] rho;

    vector[4] d[3,2];

    a ~ normal(0,1) T[0,];

I didn't check the Java program in, but I have it in
case anyone else needs it for something.

- Bob

For Mac users, please try install RStan as

install.packages('rstan', repos = 'http://wiki.stan.googlecode.com/git/R')

If this is successful, we could try to use RStan as

library(rstan)
schools.code <- '
 data {
   int[0,] J; // number of schools
    real y[J]; // estimated treatment effects
   real[0,] sigma_y[J]; // s.e. of effect estimates
  }
  parameters {
   real theta[J];
    real mu;
    real[0,] tau;
  }
  model {
   theta ~ normal(mu, tau);
    y ~ normal(theta, sigma_y);
 }
'

dat <- list(J = 8,
            y = c(28,  8, -3,  7, -1,  1, 18, 12),
           sigma_y = c(15, 10, 16, 11,  9, 11, 10, 18))

fit <- stan(model.code = schools.code, data = dat,
            n.iter = 2012, n.chains = 4)

The above should work, but as I have not got my Mac to try it.  If it goes well, we are very close to let Andrew try it.

Thanks,
Jiqiang

